<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baranja</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baranja is a historical region in the Pannonian Plain between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drava">Drava</a>, divided since 1920 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>. Its southern part passed to the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, was annexed by Hungary in 1941–1944, and now forms part of Croatia's Osijek-Baranja County, while the northern part remains Hungarian.</p></div>
